# Client rules for subscriptions and the inboxes that receive notifications (LWS core and
# lws10-notifications-webhook) (YAML-LD, format 0.11.0).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: Subscriptions, as a client makes them, and notifications, as its inbox receives them
comment: >-
  What the subscription requests a client POSTs to the session's NotificationService must carry,
  and how the client's inbox must treat the notifications the session delivers to it. The session
  advertises one subscription type, WebhookSubscription, and signs every notification with the
  key its storage description publishes, unless a task makes it forge one. A delivery is the
  session's request and the inbox's answer (OBSERVATION.md section 3).
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/
  - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/
entries:
  - id: "#client-subscription-media-type"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-subscription-media-type
    label: The client sends a subscription request as an application/lws+json object
    comment: >-
      A body conforms to a media type when it is labelled with it and parses as it. The clause
      also says the POST is authenticated; that is not judged per request, because a client may
      first try without a token and authenticate after the 401, as discovery works.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscriptions
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-create-post-lws-json
    observe:
      role: subscriptions
      method: POST
    expect:
      contentType: application/lws+json
      json:
        - pointer: ""
          jsonType: object
    guidance: >-
      POST the subscription as a JSON object with "Content-Type: application/lws+json".

  - id: "#client-subscription-type"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-subscription-type
    label: The client's subscription requests have a type the NotificationService advertises
    comment: >-
      The session's NotificationService lists one subscriptionType, WebhookSubscription, so
      that is the only type that passes.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-request
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#webhook-subscription
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#subscription-type
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-required-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-type
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/subscription-type-and-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/subscription-type-identifier
    observe:
      role: subscriptions
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /type
          equals: WebhookSubscription
    guidance: >-
      Read the subscriptionType array of the NotificationService in the storage description,
      and set "type" to one of its values: here, "WebhookSubscription".

  - id: "#client-subscription-topic"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-subscription-topic
    label: The client's subscription requests have a topic array of URIs
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#subscription-request
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-required-fields
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/subscription-request-topic
    observe:
      role: subscriptions
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /topic
          jsonType: array
        - pointer: /topic
          every:
            - pointer: ""
              jsonType: string
              matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Set "topic" to an array of the URLs of the resources to hear about, even when there is
      only one.

  - id: "#client-subscription-inbox"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-subscription-inbox
    label: The client's webhook subscription requests name an inbox URI
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#webhook-subscription
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/subscription-inbox-required
    observe:
      role: subscriptions
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /type
          equals: WebhookSubscription
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /inbox
          jsonType: string
          matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Set "inbox" to the URL the server is to deliver notifications to.

  - id: "#client-subscription-own-inbox"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-subscription-own-inbox
    label: Each of the client's webhook subscriptions has an inbox URL of its own
    comment: >-
      A permission, so the rule is informational: an inbox shared between subscriptions lets the
      notification server tell that they belong together.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#privacy-considerations
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/per-subscription-inbox-urls
    observe:
      role: subscriptions
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /inbox
          jsonType: string
    expect:
      inboxShared: false
    guidance: >-
      To keep the server from linking your subscriptions, give each its own inbox URL, such as one
      with a random path segment.

  # ---- the inbox: genuine and forged notifications (format 0.11.0) ----

  - id: "#client-inbox-acknowledges-genuine-delivery"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-inbox-acknowledges-genuine-delivery
    label: The client's inbox acknowledges a genuine notification with a 2xx
    comment: >-
      A notification the session signed with its published key verifies by the steps of section
      5.2, and "a 2xx response indicates successful receipt". An inbox may refuse one for reasons
      of its own, such as a 410 to end a subscription, so a refusal is a warning, not a failure.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#signature-verification
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#webhook-delivery
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/receiver-verification-steps
    observe:
      role: delivery
      deliverySignature: genuine
      statusCode: [2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    expect:
      statusCode: 2xx
    guidance: >-
      Answer a notification whose signature verifies with a 2xx. If your inbox refuses genuine
      notifications, check how it rebuilds the signature base: the components are @method, @scheme,
      @authority and @path of the inbox URL as subscribed, then content-type and content-digest.

  - id: "#client-inbox-refuses-unpublished-key"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-inbox-refuses-unpublished-key
    label: The client's inbox refuses a notification signed with a key the storage description does not publish
    comment: >-
      The keyid names the published key, but the signature was made with another. Only an inbox
      that verifies the signature with the published key notices.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#webhook-authentication
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#signature-verification
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/inbox-verifies-signature
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/receiver-verification-steps
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Change a resource one of your subscriptions covers. The session signs that notification
        with a key its storage description does not publish.
      arm: forgedUnpublishedKey
    observe:
      role: delivery
      deliverySignature: unpublishedKey
      statusCode: [2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    expect:
      statusCode: [3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    guidance: >-
      Verify every notification's signature with the verification method its keyid names in the
      storage description, and refuse it, with a 401 for instance, when it does not verify.

  - id: "#client-inbox-refuses-altered-body"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-inbox-refuses-altered-body
    label: The client's inbox refuses a notification whose body no longer matches its signed Content-Digest
    comment: >-
      The signature covers the body only through content-digest (RFC 9421 section 7.2.8), so
      verifying it includes checking that the body has that digest (RFC 9530). The session signs
      the notification, then changes its body.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#webhook-authentication
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#signature-requirements
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/inbox-verifies-signature
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Change a resource one of your subscriptions covers. The session signs that notification,
        then alters its body.
      arm: forgedAlteredBody
    observe:
      role: delivery
      deliverySignature: alteredBody
      statusCode: [2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    expect:
      statusCode: [3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    guidance: >-
      Compute the SHA-256 of the body you received and compare it with the Content-Digest the
      signature covers; refuse the notification when they differ.

  - id: "#client-inbox-refuses-keyid-without-fragment"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-inbox-refuses-keyid-without-fragment
    label: The client's inbox refuses a notification whose keyid is not a URL with a fragment
    comment: >-
      The signature verifies with the published key, but the keyid is the storage's URL alone. The
      first step of section 5.2 requires a fragment, which names the verification method.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#signature-verification
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/receiver-verification-steps
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Change a resource one of your subscriptions covers. The session gives that notification a
        keyid without a fragment.
      arm: forgedKeyidWithoutFragment
    observe:
      role: delivery
      deliverySignature: keyidWithoutFragment
      statusCode: [2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    expect:
      statusCode: [3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    guidance: >-
      Refuse a notification whose keyid has no fragment. Do not fall back to the storage
      description's only key, or its first.

  - id: "#client-inbox-refuses-foreign-key-document"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-inbox-refuses-foreign-key-document
    label: The client's inbox refuses a notification whose keyid names a document that is not the storage description it claims to be
    comment: >-
      The keyid names a document under the storage whose id is the storage's URL, not its own, and
      which publishes a key of its own. Anyone who can write a resource under a storage could
      publish one. The third step of section 5.2 requires the document's id to match the keyid's
      URL.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/#signature-verification
    traits: [Post, Notifications]
    area: notifications
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-notifications-webhook/receiver-verification-steps
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Change a resource one of your subscriptions covers. The session signs that notification
        with a key from a document that only claims to be the storage description.
      arm: forgedForeignKeyDocument
    observe:
      role: delivery
      deliverySignature: foreignKeyDocument
      statusCode: [2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    expect:
      statusCode: [3xx, 4xx, 5xx]
    guidance: >-
      Dereference the keyid's URL without its fragment, and refuse the notification unless the
      document's top-level id is exactly that URL.
